titre$ Key to the species of Lactarius- Gro Gulden
com$ Gro Gulden A preliminary guide to the macromycetes in the Finse area / GF 2011
1,0 $ Milk persistently white, pileus brown, papillate $ L. nanus
1,2 $ Milk initially white, changing sooner or later to violet, pileus yellow to (purplish) brown
2,3 $ Pileus yellow, without brown colours
2,5 $ Pileus entirely violaceous to purplish brown or mixed with yellow
3,0 $ Pileus margin tomented-hairy $ L. dryadophilus
3,4 $ Pileus margin smooth, not hairy
4,0 $ Lamella white to cream, paler than pileus $ L. salicis-herbaceae
4,0 $ Lamellae cream- to peach-coloured, darker than pileus $ L. salicis-reticulatae
5,0 $ Lamellae cream to yellow, pileus often with yellow patches $ L. pseudouvidus
5,0 $ Lamellae white, pileus without any yellow, often papillate $ L. brunneoviolaceus
